# Day 3 - Git, GitHub & Test Documentation

## Objective
To learn Git and GitHub for managing test artifacts, maintaining test documentation, collaborating with teams, and version controlling test cases.

---

## Tools Used
- Git
- GitHub
- GitHub Desktop (Optional)

---

## Topics Covered

### 1. Git & GitHub Basics
Learned the purpose of version control and how Git helps track and manage testing artifacts.

---

### 2. Git Environment Setup
Completed:
- Git installation
- Git configuration (username and email)
- GitHub account setup
- Repository creation

---

### 3. Git Commands Practiced
Practiced commonly used Git commands:
- `git init`
- `git clone`
- `git add`
- `git commit`
- `git push`
- `git pull`
- `git fetch`

Also learned:
- `.gitignore`
- Commit message conventions

---

### 4. Branching Strategy
Understood Git branching concepts:
- `feature/test-login`
- `bugfix/login-validation`

Learned to:
- Create branches for features
- Work independently
- Merge after review

---

### 5. Test Repository Organization
Created organized repository structure:

```text
/test-project
 ├── test-cases/
 │   ├── functional/
 │   ├── integration/
 │   ├── regression/
 ├── test-data/
 ├── bug-reports/
